{
  "scope": "Two immutable independent native classic-note sources, eight actual pinned Calc cell cuts/sorts with data identity proof and official XSD/OPC. Raw newly created target sheets introduce styled header/footer controls outside the SDK's declared basic print-band support; both original producer files remain unsupported negative cases. Six positive outputs use same-sheet edits or explicitly select the original native page style on the new target before moving data, without patching output bytes. Both VML and commentPr are recorded before editing; producer loss/normalization remains explicit. SDK preserves both sources and physically transports boxes with valid mapped note cells, retaining extents and native/body identities. Synthetic core point metrics are separate from fixed-font browser/native geometry acceptance. Excel/WPS structural runtime unverified.",
  "references": [
    "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/documentformat.openxml.drawing.spreadsheet.onecellanchor?view=openxml-3.0.1",
    "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/documentformat.openxml.drawing.spreadsheet.editasvalues?view=openxml-3.0.1",
    "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/documentformat.openxml.vml.spreadsheet.resizewithcells?view=openxml-3.0.1"
  ],
  "office": "LibreOffice 25.8.1.1 54047653041915e595ad4e45cccea684809c77b5",
